35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The receipts show 2,300 yen monthly, often duplicated. The office cleaner costs 4,200 yen per hour, billed to one tenant.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"One hundred and two minutes total. And the grout fails in eleven days. That’s not a task, it’s a recurring tax on my time.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The kitchen mess comes from three people, yet the calendar shows two are gone weekly. The work doesn’t match the presence.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Midori, the previous tenants’ note is a warning. Permanent splits led to silence. I need a shared standard, not just my own guess.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@May, the chat logs show our fights start with reminders. The grout fails in eleven days. We need a system that prevents that silence.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, 102 minutes at 4,200 yen is 428,400 yen monthly. That is far more than our 2,300 yen in supplies.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, that math assumes we hire for every minute. I need to know if outsourcing removes the 102 minutes from my schedule, or just adds management time.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, the calendar shows two of us are gone for weeks. If the work is fixed, the absent ones are free-riding. I need the labor to track presence.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, presence is one thing, but the standard is another. If ""done"" means different things to us, the room is never actually finished.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. The reminders cause the fights. If we define ""done"" clearly, we stop the cycle.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, the office bills one tenant upfront. That creates a debt. I need to know who holds that risk before we commit.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, the risk is real, but the time is the killer. 102 minutes is a significant chunk of my week. I need to know if outsourcing actually removes that burden or just shifts it.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the debt is a symptom. The calendar proves two people vanish for weeks. If the work is fixed, they pay nothing. I need the labor to track presence.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, presence matters, but the previous tenants proved permanent splits kill relationships. I need a shared standard so ""done"" means the same thing for everyone.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. The reminders cause the fights. If we define ""done"" clearly, we stop the cycle.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
